WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.056 --> 00:00:02.166
- We're at the BuzzFeed holiday party

00:00:02.166 --> 00:00:04.024
We'll see how it goes!

00:00:04.024 --> 00:00:05.632
Cheers!

00:00:05.632 --> 00:00:08.132
(party music)

00:00:18.127 --> 00:00:21.543
(cricket chirping)

00:00:21.543 --> 00:00:22.729
(squeaky hinge)

00:00:22.729 --> 00:00:25.228
(upbeat music)

00:00:25.228 --> 00:00:28.986
The BuzzFeed holiday party is a grand old

00:00:28.986 --> 00:00:31.204
tradition where you all get shit faced.

00:00:31.204 --> 00:00:33.496
- I had many tequila shots,

00:00:33.496 --> 00:00:34.580
- They don't do shots

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:36.274
- I know, we went to
a bar after the party.

00:00:36.274 --> 00:00:37.300
- Oh my god.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:39.205
- These lights feel loud.

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:40.621
- I might just still be drunk.

00:00:40.621 --> 00:00:42.300
- I don't know if these clothes match.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:45.469
- In my ideal world, I would've stayed in,

00:00:45.469 --> 00:00:47.024
ordered take-out...

00:00:47.024 --> 00:00:49.839
- I just need something
greasy, something unhealthy

00:00:49.839 --> 00:00:52.706
- I know that food after
drinking, a lot of times

00:00:52.706 --> 00:00:55.440
can make me feel not great.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:58.683
- So we'll see how this
goes, how it rides.

00:00:58.683 --> 00:01:01.100
(soft music)

00:01:03.217 --> 00:01:05.495
- Oh, it smells fucking amazing.

00:01:05.495 --> 00:01:07.915
- I feel like this is
healthy and good for you.

00:01:07.915 --> 00:01:10.898
- Mm, I don't know how I feel about that.

00:01:10.898 --> 00:01:11.815
- Oh I love that.

00:01:11.815 --> 00:01:12.915
- Oh that's so good.

00:01:12.915 --> 00:01:13.748
- It's lovely.

00:01:13.748 --> 00:01:16.707
- It's warming me from the
inside out, that's probably good.

00:01:16.707 --> 00:01:19.562
- My throats hurts so bad
because of all the screaming,

00:01:19.562 --> 00:01:20.854
this is like really nice.

00:01:20.854 --> 00:01:21.764
- Very soothing.

00:01:21.764 --> 00:01:24.262
- I wish I was on my couch
or in my bed drinking this,

00:01:24.262 --> 00:01:25.534
not here.

00:01:25.534 --> 00:01:27.951
(soft music)

00:01:29.313 --> 00:01:31.017
- Just saying, if I see
something white and runny

00:01:31.017 --> 00:01:32.540
this early in the morning,

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:34.850
I'd tell him to get out.

00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:35.863
(ding)

00:01:35.863 --> 00:01:38.223
- I love congee, I mean it's
basically like porridge.

00:01:38.223 --> 00:01:42.049
- I don't know how my
stomach feels about this.

00:01:42.049 --> 00:01:44.637
- Makes me feel better without making me

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:45.872
feel like I'm gonna be sick.

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:47.502
- This is like healthy hangover food.

00:01:47.502 --> 00:01:49.771
- I actually don't hate it.

00:01:49.771 --> 00:01:50.878
(laughs)

00:01:50.878 --> 00:01:52.610
It tastes kinda good.

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:53.969
- Hmm.

00:01:53.969 --> 00:01:55.393
- When you're hungover, you want to do

00:01:55.393 --> 00:01:56.940
minimal amount of chewing.

00:01:56.940 --> 00:01:58.892
- Well I'm all about swallowing.

00:01:58.892 --> 00:02:00.975
(laughs)

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:04.623
(upbeat music)

00:02:05.622 --> 00:02:07.797
- Oh yeah, I recognize this tea.

00:02:07.797 --> 00:02:10.731
- Oh, green tea, I love green tea, yes!

00:02:10.731 --> 00:02:13.568
- It's not like snapping me
out of my hangover right now.

00:02:13.568 --> 00:02:15.120
- It's like a punch in the face.

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:16.435
(laughs)

00:02:16.435 --> 00:02:18.235
- Oh this is nice. This is nice.

00:02:18.235 --> 00:02:21.065
Can I live here? Can I just
move in right here to this spot?

00:02:21.065 --> 00:02:22.637
- I love it. It's delicious.

00:02:22.637 --> 00:02:25.173
I feel healthy. Balanced.

00:02:25.173 --> 00:02:27.821
Basically gonna start a fitness blog now.

00:02:27.821 --> 00:02:30.707
(upbeat music)

00:02:30.707 --> 00:02:31.929
- Oh, this is uh..

00:02:31.929 --> 00:02:34.030
(speaks foreign language)

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:34.863
- Oh, wow

00:02:36.108 --> 00:02:37.956
- It's basically vegetables, meats,

00:02:37.956 --> 00:02:40.109
kimchi, and something else.

00:02:40.109 --> 00:02:41.509
- This is more my jam right here.

00:02:41.509 --> 00:02:42.346
- Wait.

00:02:42.346 --> 00:02:43.309
- This is my jam.

00:02:43.309 --> 00:02:45.699
- Are those little blood cubes?

00:02:45.699 --> 00:02:47.183
- Excuse me?

00:02:47.183 --> 00:02:48.669
- What is a blood cube?

00:02:48.669 --> 00:02:50.542
- What do you think a blood cube is?

00:02:50.542 --> 00:02:52.404
- I don't know if it's because

00:02:52.404 --> 00:02:54.432
I just grew up with this,
but this hits the spot.

00:02:54.432 --> 00:02:56.487
- Oh yeah, it's spicy, yes!

00:02:56.487 --> 00:02:58.077
This is what I needed.

00:02:58.077 --> 00:02:59.628
- I don't know if I feel less hungover.

00:02:59.628 --> 00:03:00.461
- Mhmm.

00:03:00.461 --> 00:03:02.638
- But it kind of was like
a nice shock to the system.

00:03:02.638 --> 00:03:05.591
- It's for sure the best hangover
food we had so far today.

00:03:05.591 --> 00:03:06.802
- [Off Screen] I gotta take
that away from you guys.

00:03:06.802 --> 00:03:08.592
(groans)

00:03:08.592 --> 00:03:10.177
- No no no, hold on

00:03:10.177 --> 00:03:11.361
(laughs)

00:03:11.361 --> 00:03:13.944
(upbeat music)

00:03:14.912 --> 00:03:16.942
- Wait, I think it sort
of smells like vodka.

00:03:16.942 --> 00:03:19.372
- If it's vodka, I'm
going to throw it at you.

00:03:19.372 --> 00:03:20.732
- [In Unison] Ooh

00:03:20.732 --> 00:03:21.684
- Coconut water.

00:03:21.684 --> 00:03:23.752
- Am I trashy for thinking
it smelled like vodka?

00:03:23.752 --> 00:03:24.585
- Mhmm.

00:03:24.585 --> 00:03:25.418
- Cheers.

00:03:25.418 --> 00:03:27.422
(glasses clink)

00:03:27.422 --> 00:03:29.320
- I thought it was gonna
taste like normal water.

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:30.480
- That's good, too.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:32.358
(talking over each other)

00:03:32.358 --> 00:03:33.206
- It's bearable.

00:03:33.206 --> 00:03:35.513
- I would just like some normal water.

00:03:35.513 --> 00:03:37.472
- All these dishes are
for sure healthier than

00:03:37.472 --> 00:03:40.158
